  "result": "Done! I've added VAT (Value Added Tax) support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Added `lineVAT(line)` function - calculates VAT on the amount AFTER discount:\n  - VAT = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n  - Rounded with `roundCents()` and clamped to \u22650\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - total = subtotal - discount + vat\n  - vat is the sum of all individual line VATs\n\n**Updated `src/render.js`:**\n- Shows VAT line in invoice text (when VAT > 0)\n- Format: \"Subtotal\" / \"Discount\" (optional) / \"VAT\" (optional) / \"Total\"\n\n**Features:**\n- VAT computed per line on amount after discount (not on total)\n- Each line's VAT is rounded independently\n- Invoice VAT is the sum of rounded line VATs (never a percentage)\n- Supports multiple VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%) on same invoice\n- Proper handling with discounts and tier discounts\n\n**Added 5 new tests** for VAT calculations:\n- lineVAT calculations with/without discounts\n- Default vatRate to 0\n- invoiceTotals with VAT\n- Multi-line VAT examples\n\n**Updated all existing tests** to account for VAT in product calculations\n\nAll 95 tests pass \u2714",
